	<Folder>
		<name>U.S. Nuclear Weapons in Europe (400 nuclear weapons)</name>
		<open>1</open>
		<description><![CDATA[During the Cold War, the United States deployed a large percentage (up to one-third) of its nuclear weapons in other countries and at sea. At its peak arsenal size in the late 1960s, the United States stored weapons in 17 different countries. The peak number of US nuclear weapons in Europe was 7,300 in 1971. <p>
The United States terminated many nuclear missions after the end of the Cold War and retired the weapons. Today, perhaps as many as 400 bombs remain at eight facilities in six European countries, the last remnant of a bygone era.
<p>
For further information on US nuclear weapons in Europe, see: http://www.nukestrat.com/us/afn/nato.htm]]></description>
